- English text: natural modern spoken English, short lines (max 12 words per bubble, one idea per bubble); contractions
  (I'm, don't), short answers and interjections like real people.
<% if %w[A1 A2].include?(cefr) -%>
- Level <%= cefr %>: high-frequency vocabulary, simple grammar (present simple and continuous, past simple, going to, can,
  have to, will for offers and promises); common phrasal verbs and fixed expressions are welcome.
<% else -%>
- Level <%= cefr %>: everyday vocabulary and grammar of this level, used naturally (no explanations inside the story).
<% end -%>
- "target_words": dictionary forms; phrasal verbs and fixed expressions count as one ("run into", "by the way", "embarrassed").
  Each target word or expression appears at least twice across the episode.
- No <%= native.name %> words inside the English text.
<% if native.code == "ru" -%>
- Russian translation: «ты» between friends, family and children, «вы» to strangers, the boss and older people.
<% end -%>
